# level start, derived with GameplayInputBranchTool from s1-complete-run.bk2 (not edited by hand):
#   GameplayInputBranchTool --input-start 61548 --resume 400 --resume-from 244
#     <s1 ROM> s1 syz 1 320 sonic none src/test/resources/traces/s1/_movies/s1-complete-run.bk2
#     247 <out> '69 R'
# Rows 0-246 are the recording (it destroys the first Crabmeat). Rows 247-315 hold Right instead
# of the recorded jump at row 248, so he runs into the second Crabmeat and is hurt at frame 260.
# The manifest holds the live rewind key for frames 280-315; rewind steps back one frame per held
# frame, so frame 316 resumes from the state after frame 243. The rows from 316 on are therefore
# the recording's rows from 244 (--resume-from 244): the retry is the recorded jump, which bounces
# on and destroys that Crabmeat. Checked: the retry matches syz1_completerun rows (frame - 72)
# on every frame from 316 to 559.
